NAME
    uniq - collapse adjacent duplicate lines

SYNOPSIS
    uniq [-c]

DESCRIPTION
    Collapses ADJACENT duplicate lines only, matching real uniq's own
    semantics - it is NOT a global dedup, so pipe through 'sort' first if
    that's what's actually wanted ('regs | sort | uniq'). -c prefixes each
    remaining line with its consecutive repeat count.

EXAMPLES
    watch log 1 | sort | uniq -c
